---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const aboutJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: 'About Annotated Papers',
  url: new URL('/about', Astro.site).toString(),
  description: 'The editorial method behind Annotated Papers by Chris Hayduk.',
  author: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: 'Chris Hayduk',
    url: 'https://chrishayduk.com',
  },
  inLanguage: 'en',
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About — Annotated Papers by Chris Hayduk"
  description="How Annotated Papers combines research papers, runnable implementations, and interactive figures."
  jsonLd={aboutJsonLd}
>
  <article class="about-page">
    <header class="about-header">
      <p class="section-label">About</p>
      <h1>About Annotated Papers</h1>
      <p class="about-lede">
        This site contains detailed annotations of research papers that I have found worth
        understanding closely. Each annotation combines the source paper, explanatory notes,
        runnable code, and interactive figures.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="about-body">
      <nav class="contents" aria-label="On this page">
        <p>On this page</p>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#purpose">Purpose</a></li>
          <li><a href="#method">Method</a></li>
          <li><a href="#provenance">Code and provenance</a></li>
          <li><a href="#current">Current annotation</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <div class="sections">
        <section id="purpose">
          <h2>Purpose</h2>
          <p>
            Research papers are concise records of new results. They often assume substantial
            background knowledge and leave implementation details to supplements or codebases.
            That economy is useful for communicating among specialists, but it can make careful
            study unnecessarily difficult.
          </p>
          <p>
            These annotations slow the reading process down. The goal is not to replace the
            original paper or reduce it to a summary, but to make the paper easier to work through
            in full. The format follows the example of
            <a href="https://nlp.seas.harvard.edu/annotated-transformer/">The Annotated Transformer</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="method">
          <h2>Method</h2>
          <p>Each annotation is organized around three related forms of evidence:</p>
          <ol class="method-list">
            <li>
              <h3>The paper</h3>
              <p>
                The argument, equations, and architecture are explained in sequence. Notation is
                kept close to the source so readers can move between the annotation and the paper.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>The implementation</h3>
              <p>
                Code excerpts come from real, runnable reimplementations rather than pseudocode.
                Variable names follow the paper, algorithm numbers are cited inline, and tensor
                shapes are checked throughout the code.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>The figures</h3>
              <p>
                Interactive figures are used where manipulating a mechanism directly is more
                informative than another paragraph of description.
              </p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section id="provenance">
          <h2>Code and provenance</h2>
          <p>
            The implementations are written for pedagogical clarity and include unit and
            integration tests. Each annotation pins its reference repository to a specific commit.
            This makes it possible to inspect the exact version used by the site, clone it, and run
            the examples locally.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="current" class="current-paper">
          <p class="section-label">Current annotation</p>
          <h2>The Annotated AlphaFold2</h2>
          <p>
            The first annotation covers AlphaFold2, including the Evoformer, Invariant Point
            Attention, FAPE, and the Structure Module. It is paired with
            <a href="https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/minAlphaFold2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">minAlphaFold2</a>,
            a roughly 8,000-line PyTorch implementation of about 95% of the paper.
          </p>
          <div class="current-links">
            <a class="primary-link" href="/alphafold2">Read the annotation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
            <a class="secondary-link" href="https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/minAlphaFold2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              View the repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>

        <footer class="author-note">
          <p>
            Annotated and implemented by <a href="https://chrishayduk.com" rel="me">Chris Hayduk</a>.
            More of my writing is available at <a href="https://chrishayduk.com" rel="me">chrishayduk.com</a>.
          </p>
        </footer>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    width: min(100% - 3rem, 70rem);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .section-label {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .about-header {
    max-width: 51rem;
    padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 7.5rem);
  }

  .about-header h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 5.5vw, 4.25rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .about-lede {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .about-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 12rem minmax(0, 42rem);
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 8rem);
    padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
  }

  .contents {
    display: block;
    align-self: start;
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .contents > p {
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .contents ol {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .contents li + li { margin-top: 0.55rem; }

  .contents a {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .contents a:hover { color: var(--accent); }

  .sections > section {
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem);
    padding-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .sections > section + section {
    padding-top: 3.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .sections h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.35rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .sections section > p:not(.section-label),
  .method-list p,
  .author-note p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .sections section > p + p { margin-top: 1.15rem; }

  .sections a:not(.primary-link, .secondary-link),
  .author-note a {
    color: var(--fg);
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .method-list {
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: method;
  }

  .method-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 1.5rem 0 1.5rem 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    counter-increment: method;
  }

  .method-list li::before {
    position: absolute;
    top: 1.7rem;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
    content: '0' counter(method);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
  }

  .method-list h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .current-paper {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .current-paper .section-label { margin-bottom: 0.85rem; }

  .current-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .current-links a {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    padding: 0 1rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .primary-link {
    background: var(--fg);
    color: var(--bg);
  }

  .primary-link:hover {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--surface-strong);
  }

  .secondary-link {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .secondary-link:hover {
    border-color: var(--rule-strong);
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .author-note {
    padding-block: 0.5rem 1rem;
  }

  .author-note p { font-size: 0.9rem; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .about-body {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2.5rem;
    }

    .contents {
      position: static;
      padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }

    .contents ol {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.55rem 1.25rem;
    }

    .contents li + li { margin-top: 0; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .about-page { width: min(100% - 2rem, 70rem); }
    .about-header { padding-block: 4rem; }
    .about-header h1 { font-size: 2.75rem; }
    .current-links { align-items: stretch; flex-direction: column; }
    .current-links a { justify-content: center; }
  }
</style>
